### Product endpoints — tested THROUGH the API Gateway (Ocelot) at :7000.
### These require a JWT. We log in first (also via the gateway) to get the token.

@gateway = http://localhost:7000

### 0. Log in to get a token
# @name login
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "student",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### Token from the login response above.
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 1. (Negative test) List products WITHOUT a token -> 401 Unauthorized
GET {{gateway}}/api/products

### 2. List all products (authorized)
GET {{gateway}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Create a product
# @name created
POST {{gateway}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "USB-C Hub",
  "description": "7-in-1 aluminium hub",
  "price": 34.5,
  "stock": 12
}

### 4. Get the product we just created by id
GET {{gateway}}/api/products/{{created.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Update that product
PUT {{gateway}}/api/products/{{created.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "USB-C Hub (v2)",
  "description": "7-in-1 aluminium hub, updated",
  "price": 39.9,
  "stock": 20
}

### 6. Delete that product -> 204 No Content
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/products/{{created.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
